ORIGINAL WORK

The Zulu A7 hardware design is an Adaptation, as defined in section 1(a) of
that licence, of the XuLA2 FPGA board.

  Original Work:    XuLA2
  Original Author:  Dave Vandenbout / XESS Corp.
  Source:           https://github.com/xesscorp/XuLA2
                    (hardware design in pcb/)
  Licence:          CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported, per the notice on the XuLA2
                    schematic

The XuLA2 schematic carries this notice on its second sheet, reproduced
here verbatim ("(c)" stands for the circled-C symbol drawn before it):

  (c) 2012, XESS Corp. Some rights reserved.
  Licensed under a Creative Commons
  Attribution-Share-Alike Unported License.
  See creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

In this repository's schematics, the General IO sheet carries the line
"2026, Christian Tambe. Some rights reserved." above the same three licence
lines. That line overwrote the XESS line during the XuLA3 rework that
preceded Zulu A7, and the schematic sheets do not yet carry the XESS line
again. This file reproduces the upstream notice, which applies to the
material that comes from XuLA2; keep it with any copy of the schematics.

Under section 8(b) of the licence, XESS Corp., as Licensor of XuLA2, offers
each recipient of Zulu A7 a licence to the original XuLA2 Work on the same
terms.


